window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-77924ca0a867efcc"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"prepare-a-business-review\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">准备业务回顾</h1> <p>将周期性 KPI、结账和预测输入整理成有来源依据的业绩说明。</p> <p>向 ChatGPT 提供 KPI 仪表板、结账工作簿、指标定义、预测更新、往期回顾和负责人笔记，然后请它在便于审阅的说明中解释重大变化、差异、异常、风险、数据质量问题和后续跟进事项。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>产品、运营、增长或财务团队的每周、每月或每季度业务回顾。</li> <li>结合 KPI 仪表板、工作簿、预测、过往汇报和负责人笔记的回顾。</li> <li>在领导层审阅前，需要让重大变化、异常以及重要数据都能追溯到来源的团队。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$documents</code></td> <td>创建并核验一份可编辑的说明文档，采用清晰的管理层结构并注明来源。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>检查结账工作簿和预测文件、核验数字，并追溯重大数据对应的来源工作表。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive（需联网）</a></td> <td>从指定的 Drive 文件或文件夹读取已批准的工作簿、往期回顾、仪表板和负责人笔记。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack（需联网）</a></td> <td>当相关信息属于本次回顾记录时，读取经批准的财务结账讨论串和负责人背景信息。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>准备业务回顾</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请使用 $documents 和 $spreadsheets，为 [weekly, monthly, or quarterly] 的 [business or team] 准备业务回顾。\n\n请使用我提供的 KPI 仪表板、指标定义、结账工作簿、收入和费用表、预测更新、往期回顾及负责人笔记。如果任何输入位于已连接的插件中，只使用我指定的确切 @google-drive 文件或 @slack 讨论串。\n\n请创建一份可编辑的文档，包含简短的领导层摘要、重大 KPI 变化、关键差异、异常、相对于预测的变化、风险、数据质量检查、审阅问题和按负责人整理的后续事项。适合时加入辅助图表。每个重要数字都应注明其对应的工作簿工作表、仪表板或来源笔记。不要填入编造的数字；请列出缺少依据的主张和缺失输入，供审阅。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://openai.com/academy/codex-for-work/how-data-science-teams-use-codex/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI Academy：数据科学团队（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">智能体技能</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"build-from-the-recurring-review-record\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">根据周期性回顾记录整理内容</h2> <p>业务回顾应解释发生了哪些变化、变化的原因，以及团队需要作出什么决定。ChatGPT 可以根据 KPI 仪表板、指标定义、结账工作簿、预测更新、往期回顾和负责人笔记整理初稿，同时保留清晰的来源路径。</p> <p><a id=\"prepare-the-review-sources\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">准备回顾所需的来源</h2> <p>明确指定 ChatGPT 应使用的文件、仪表板和对话。提供汇报期间、受众、重要性阈值、上一版预测以及任何必需章节。如果回顾应基于一组经过控制且已批准的输入，请避免让 ChatGPT 在已连接的工作区中进行宽泛搜索。</p> <ol> <li>定义回顾期间、受众和重要性阈值。</li> <li>附上 KPI 仪表板、指标定义、相关工作簿、预测更新、往期回顾和负责人笔记。</li> <li>请 ChatGPT 在起草前检查数据质量，并追溯重要数字的来源。</li> <li>运行起始提示词，并审查变化、差异、异常、风险、假设和后续跟进事项。</li> <li>在回顾进入领导层讨论前，确认来源链接和负责人行动项。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"review-the-narrative\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">审查业绩说明</h2> <p>有用的初稿会把有依据的结论与仍需负责人回答的问题区分开来。它应指出重大的 KPI 变化和相对预测的变动，用浅显的语言解释风险，并让后续事项容易分派。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Compare this business review with the prior review and audit the narrative.\n\nShow:\n\n- newly material KPI changes and variances\n- anomalies that resolved or worsened\n- risks and owner follow-ups that remain open\n- metrics whose definitions or sources changed\n- unsupported claims or data-quality issues\n- questions the team should ask next\n\nCite the source behind every material comparison, flag uncertainty, and keep unresolved items grouped by owner.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">请将这次业务复盘与上一次复盘比较，并审查其中的叙述。\n\n说明：\n\n- 新出现的重要 KPI 变化和差异\n- 已经解决或变得更严重的异常\n- 尚未消除的风险和负责人跟进事项\n- 定义或来源发生变化的指标\n- 缺少支持的主张或数据质量问题\n- 团队接下来应该提出的问题\n\n为每项重要比较引用其背后的来源，标明不确定性，并按负责人归类保留尚未解决的事项。</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"prepare-a-business-review\">Prepare a business review</h1> <p>Turn recurring KPI, close, and forecast inputs into a sourced performance narrative.</p> <p>Give ChatGPT KPI dashboards, close workbooks, metric definitions, forecast updates, prior reviews, and owner notes, then ask it to explain material changes, variances, anomalies, risks, data-quality issues, and follow-ups in a review-ready narrative.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Weekly, monthly, or quarterly business reviews for product, operations, growth, or finance teams.</li> <li>Reviews that combine KPI dashboards, workbooks, forecasts, prior reporting, and owner notes.</li> <li>Teams that need material changes, anomalies, and every important figure tied to a source before leadership review.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$documents</code></td> <td>Create and verify an editable narrative document with a clear executive structure and source notes.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>Inspect close workbooks and forecast files, validate figures, and trace material numbers to their source tabs.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive (online)</a></td> <td>Read approved workbooks, prior reviews, dashboards, and owner notes from exact Drive files or folders.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack (online)</a></td> <td>Read approved finance-close threads and owner context when those messages are part of the review record.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Prepare the business review</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $documents and $spreadsheets to prepare the [weekly, monthly, or quarterly] business review for [business or team].\n\nUse the KPI dashboard, metric definitions, close workbook, revenue and expense tables, forecast update, prior review, and owner notes I provide. If any inputs are in connected plugins, use only the exact @google-drive files or @slack threads I name.\n\nCreate an editable document with a short leadership summary, material KPI changes, key variances, anomalies, changes since forecast, risks, data-quality checks, review questions, and follow-ups by owner. Include supporting charts where useful. Cite the workbook tab, dashboard, or source note behind every material number. Do not fill gaps with invented figures; list unsupported claims and missing inputs for review.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://openai.com/academy/codex-for-work/how-data-science-teams-use-codex/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI Academy: Data science teams (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Agent skills</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"build-from-the-recurring-review-record\">Build from the recurring review record</h2> <p>A business review should explain what changed, why it changed, and what the team needs to decide. ChatGPT can assemble the first draft from KPI dashboards, metric definitions, close workbooks, forecast updates, prior reviews, and owner notes while keeping the source trail visible.</p> <h2 id=\"prepare-the-review-sources\">Prepare the review sources</h2> <p>Name the exact files, dashboards, and conversations ChatGPT should use. Include the reporting period, audience, materiality thresholds, prior forecast, and any required sections. Avoid broad searches across a connected workspace when the review should rely on a controlled set of approved inputs.</p> <ol> <li>Define the review period, audience, and materiality threshold.</li> <li>Attach the KPI dashboard, metric definitions, relevant workbooks, forecast update, prior review, and owner notes.</li> <li>Ask ChatGPT to check data quality and trace material numbers before drafting.</li> <li>Run the starter prompt and review changes, variances, anomalies, risks, assumptions, and follow-ups.</li> <li>Confirm the source links and owner actions before the review enters leadership discussion.</li> </ol> <h2 id=\"review-the-narrative\">Review the narrative</h2> <p>A useful draft separates supported conclusions from questions that still need an owner. It should call out material KPI movement and changes since forecast, explain risks in plain language, and make follow-ups easy to assign.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Compare this business review with the prior review and audit the narrative.\n\nShow:\n\n- newly material KPI changes and variances\n- anomalies that resolved or worsened\n- risks and owner follow-ups that remain open\n- metrics whose definitions or sources changed\n- unsupported claims or data-quality issues\n- questions the team should ask next\n\nCite the source behind every material comparison, flag uncertainty, and keep unresolved items grouped by owner.\n</code></pre>"};
